From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ken Russell <kbr@chromium.org>
Date: Thu, 16 Jul 2026 15:51:55 -0700
Subject: [gpu] Add pack_large_row_length_separately_pack_buffer workaround

When packing into a pixel pack buffer with a very large stride,
temporarily reset the driver's GL_PACK_ROW_LENGTH and read back pixels
row-by-row. Apply this workaround to Mali drivers.

Workaround was ported to the validating command decoder from ANGLE.

Co-authored with Gemini.

TAG: agy
CONV: 00e8b985-f726-4445-86d5-e26b326cf4f3
Test: gl_tests --gtest_filter=*PackLargeRowLength*
Test: gpu_unittests --gtest_filter=*ReadPixels2LargeRowLengthWorkaround*
Bug: 529867799
Change-Id: I417b398e77031fcefcf60808c9a9b3dabc53e3ba
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8104079
Auto-Submit: Kenneth Russell <kbr@chromium.org>
